      "writtenOn": "2023-12-20T17:42:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this is not resolved. The code added makeHandlerThread and thread_sleep to dependencies. Tests make use of makeHandlerThread, returning a regular thread, which doesn\u0027t prevent the test from sleeping.\n\nInstead, tests should change thread_sleep behaviour to not sleep. makeHandlerThread is not needed, because thread_sleep calls Thread.sleep(): this call refers to the current thread, which is the handler thread.\n\nUse threadSleep (camelCase) instead of thread_sleep.",
      "parentUuid": "e7a38986_d6d842c9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 166,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "7f64420d8356f5e6e2592bda4fb74319a7d49eb8",
